Include <limits.h> in the OpenSSL backend files that use INT_MAX.

b83ecd1 (2025-01-17, PR cisco/libsrtp#743) added INT_MAX checks to aes_gcm_ossl.c,
aes_icm_ossl.c and hmac_ossl.c without including <limits.h>. OpenSSL's <openssl/evp.h> pulls
it in; BoringSSL's does not, so against BoringSSL 26584e7a10 all three files fail with "use of
undeclared identifier 'INT_MAX'", for wasm32-wasip1 and x86_64 glibc alike. Build fix only, no
behaviour change; the build is the test.
Not fixed upstream as of 052aa2965e (main, 2026-11-13).

Upstream: none found; closed issue cisco/libsrtp#744 is a different BoringSSL build problem
(the CMake OpenSSL version check).

diff --git a/crypto/cipher/aes_gcm_ossl.c b/crypto/cipher/aes_gcm_ossl.c
index 9362a20..943637a 100644
